  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species attains a total length of 15-18 cm. Besides the bright red eye, the most striking feature is the pretty brown-red lower lappet of the caudal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The water temperature should be a bit higher than usual, 25-29°C are ideal. In the natural habitat, the water is only slightly acidic or even alkaline, so there is no need for a low pH; to the contrary, one should avoid a pH lower than 6.5.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lasiancistrus, in general, are good algae-eaters and fit in any community tank of appropriate size.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Like almost all species of ancistrine catfish, this species is a cave-brooder. A clutch of eggs found in the wild contained about 200 eggs and was deposited in a cave in a tree lying under water. The male guards the eggs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/lasiancistrus_heteracanthus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lasiancistrus: Latin, means \"shaggy ancistrus\", referring to the skin-spines (odontodes). heteracanthus: ancient Greek, means \"with aberrant spines\".</p>"
    }
  ],
